# AMD'S VENDORED FILES AND THE SHADER HEADERS MADE FROM THEM ARE KEPT BYTE FOR BYTE (2026-10-06, the own build of
# AMD's frame generation, stage 1a).
#
# This repository is used with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites the line endings of every text file on checkout.
# AMD's files at tag v2.3.0 have LF endings, and external/ffx/MANIFEST-ffx_api_2.3.0.txt holds each one to the id
# git gives its bytes in AMD's own repository: a checkout that turned LF into CRLF would fail that check on every
# file. The generated headers under ffx-own/shaders are compared byte for byte with a regeneration
# (tools/ffx-own/gen_shaders.py --verify), and the generator writes LF.
#
# "-text" means no conversion in either direction: what is committed is what is on disk. It changes nothing else
# (the files still diff as text).
#
# THE EIGHT HEADERS THAT WERE IN ffx_api_2.3.0 BEFORE THIS RULE (the ones dlssiv-helper.exe compiles against) were
# committed as AMD's LF bytes all along, and checked out as CRLF. A working tree older than this file still has them
# as CRLF, and git does not say so: it trusts what it remembers of each file, git status shows nothing for the 8 (so
# no build is stamped "-dirty" by them), and "git checkout -- external/ffx/ffx_api_2.3.0" rewrites nothing (the review
# of 2026-10-06, R1.4; this comment said the opposite before). What writes them again as committed: DELETE the folder
# external/ffx/ffx_api_2.3.0, and then, from src/DLSS-IV,
#     git checkout -- external/ffx/ffx_api_2.3.0
# tools/ffx-own/ffx_manifest.py names exactly that case and that cure. The helper's object file is the same either
# way (docs/reports/fg-3/own-build-2026-10-06/stage-1a, "helper-unchanged").
# (2026-10-28) EVERY OTHER TEXT FILE IS CHECKED OUT CRLF, whatever core.autocrlf says: the build reads the cfg, the shader
# headers and the kit's scripts with CRLF, and a clone with LF endings failed at check-cfg and read every shader header as
# stale (the public export's dry build). The rules below, later, keep AMD's files and the generated headers byte for byte.
* text=auto eol=crlf
external/ffx/ffx_api_2.3.0/** -text
ffx-own/shaders/** -text
# THE HEADERS OF THE PRODUCT'S CUTS (the own build's stage 3, 2026-10-10) are generated files too, compared byte for
# byte with a regeneration from the cut copy of AMD's source (tools/ffx-own/cuts.py --verify). The cuts themselves
# (ffx-own/cuts) are read with either line ending: their digest and their edits are taken with the endings as LF.
ffx-own/shaders-cut/** -text
# THE HEADERS OF THE PRODUCT'S ACCEPTED PICTURE CUTS (2026-10-12): the headers of the product that differ from the exact
# library's, generated and compared the same way (tools/ffx-own/cuts.py gen and --verify).
ffx-own/shaders-picture/** -text
